.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt UNIQ 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uniq
.Nd select adjacent groups of equal lines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cduiz
.Op Fl f Ar fields
.Op Fl s Ar characters
.Op Fl w Ar count
.Op Ar input Op Ar output
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Reduce each adjacent run of equal lines to one line by default.
Equal lines separated by different lines remain separate groups;
use
.Xr sort 1
first when global grouping is wanted.
.Fl c
prefixes each group with its count.
.Fl d
prints only repeated groups and
.Fl u
only groups occurring once.
.Fl i
compares without letter case.
.Fl f Ar fields
skips fields before comparing,
.Fl s Ar characters
skips characters after skipped fields, and
.Fl w Ar count
limits the comparison width.
.Fl z
uses NUL-terminated records.
.Pp
Read standard input when input is omitted or
.Ql - .
Write standard output when output is omitted or
.Ql - ;
a named output is created or truncated and needs writable authority.
Do not use the same path for input and output: opening output can destroy
unread input.
This is stream processing, not a transactional file edit.
See
.Xr sync 1
for a barrier after writing a named output.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on successful processing; nonzero for invalid options or
input/output failure. Diagnostics use standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uniq -c /etc/words.txt
cat /etc/words.txt | uniq | wc -l
.Ed
.Sh ABSD PROFILE
This is the unmodified uutils 0.12.0 utility pinned by the platform build.
The reference describes selected source-supported options; use
.Fl Fl help
for the complete upstream interface.
File access uses the process's ABSD filesystem view, output uses its
inherited stream, and the command acquires no additional authority.
There are no native Unix processes, signals or permission bits underneath
this port.
The command matrix exercises the example forms below; other options
listed here are source-checked, not separately guest-qualified.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sort 1 ,
.Xr sync 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
